+ * animation channel target is written onto its owning object as the referenced
+ * array's index plus one, stored through a pointer. Storing index + 1 (rather
+ * than index) leaves a NULL pointer meaning "no reference" while still letting
+ * index 0 be representable. cgltf_fixup_pointers walks the parsed model and
+ * turns every one of those staged indices back into a real pointer.
